# ==============================================================
# OCEAN PUZZLE - INSTRUCTIONS: ROOM 3 (Symbol Values)
# ==============================================================
# Script type : interact
# Bind to     : [FILL IN: x y z of the clickable head block]
# Map/area    : [FILL IN: map name / room]
# Import      : /s i i <paste URL>, then click the head block
#
# What it does:
#   The Oracle explains the symbol value grid puzzle in metaphor
#   (see Ocean_Puzzle_Room3_Grids.md for the real rules).
#   Speech lasts about 16 seconds. Can be replayed once every
#   45 seconds per player.
#
# Requires: puzzle1 namespace (see Submit script header)
#
# Related scripts: Instructions Rooms 1-2 and 4 (share the same cooldown)
# ==============================================================
@using puzzle1
@define Long now = system::currentTimeMillis()

@if oracle_ready_at > now
    @define Long seconds = (oracle_ready_at - now + 999L) / 1000L
    @player &cOracle: You must wait {{seconds}} seconds to hear the instructions again.
    @return
@fi

@var oracle_ready_at = now + 45000L

@player &3Oracle: &bYou have learned the voice of every sign. Now learn its worth.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bWithin each sign sleeps a number. Five walls guard the secret.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bWhere a row ends and a column settles, the waters gather into one.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bThe currents never change from wall to wall. What binds one binds all.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bDo not mistake a pattern for a law until every wall agrees.
